  41:     - The other foreground color forms one 4-connected 2x2-bbox sprite in each occupied lattice cell.
  42: 
  43:     Rule
  44:     - Keep the marker lattice fixed and clear the original sprite pixels.
  45:     - For each sprite, find the lattice marker immediately above-left of its cell.
  46:     - Repaint the same sprite shape with its bbox upper-left at half a lattice pitch down and right from that marker.
  47: 
  48:     Key insight
  49:     - The markers define identical cells; the sprite's shape matters, but its off-center position inside the cell is normalized to the cell center.
